/etc/init.d will contain the scripts these scripts can be both sourced / executed.

at the end of each runlevel scripts in /etc/rcn.d will be run. (where n is the run level being entered). Runlevel
S corresponds to bootlevel.

typically you can control the symbolic links between /etc/rcn.d to /etc/init.d using update-rc.d.

for example

update-rc.d -f vmware remove 

this will remove the vmware symbolic links in the different rc.d directories